  "period_note": "Solo (standalone, not consolidated) basis throughout, per project standing rule. Classified investments jump sharply this year (3,799m in FY2016 to 10,451m, NPL ratio 3.64%->8.29%[calculated;see below]) - this is the single largest one-year NPL deterioration in the pre-2024 series. NPL ratio: self-computed as classified_loans/gross_loans (10,451/126,138.03=8.29%) since the bank's own later highlights tables disagree with each other for this same year (FY2019 report's table shows 8.44% for FY2017; FY2021 report's table shows a materially lower 7.42% for the same FY2017, implying a larger, likely Consolidated-inclusive-of-brokerage-margin-loans, loans denominator in the later table). CRAR 14.18% (Solo) confirmed identically in Directors' Report prose and formal Pillar-3 disclosure (consolidated 13.96% in both) - no discrepancy this year.",
